      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "The sole gap in the trace is a 428-second dropout inside the KPE tunnel, far over POL-RD-07's 90-second limb, so the trace is impaired for policy purposes. POL-RD-07(i) then fixes the excess across that stretch as the straight line between the bounding fixes — the reading most favourable to the driver — producing the same 21.2 km total, still under the POL-RD-01 gate. No surface-route figure appears in the trace, and nothing in the bundle supports the 25.50 km hypothesis. Disclosed: EV-GPS-00110 is IMPAIRED (GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE) at weight 0.39.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "gaps[0].duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-08 places the initial burden on the rider to show an excess above the POL-RD-01 threshold, measured from an unimpaired trace or from an independent source of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names. The rider does neither: her claim concedes she 'did not watch the route' and states no measurement at all, and every distance figure in the bundle is the trace or a copy of it. Disclosed: the trace, EV-GPS-00110, is IMPAIRED (GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE) at weight 0.39.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00110", "EV-TRIP-00110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.thresholds.threshold_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "No independent source corroborates any detour. The chat log records the driver announcing 'going KPE ah boss' — the KPE, which trip_record.optimal_route_source confirms lies on the optimal corridor ('optimal is KPE then ECP') — and the rider answering 'ok'; nothing admits a diversion, and the export was truncated before any later messages. Disclosed: EV-CHAT-00110 is IMPAIRED (TRUNCATED_LOG) at weight 0.6, and EV-FARE-00110's distance_charged_km of 21.20 copies the trace figure, so it is not independent corroboration under POL-RD-07(ii).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00110", "EV-FARE-00110", "EV-TRIP-00110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing falls to be corrected under POL-RD-09(4). The $3.00 of ERP charged equals the trip record's optimal_route_erp_sgd of $3.00 on the KPE-ECP optimal route, so it is a pass-through on the corridor actually optimal, not a phantom gantry the trace never crossed. Disclosed: EV-FARE-00110 is IMPAIRED (PARTIAL_RECORD) at weight 0.75; the absent gantry itemisation is a record gap, not a wrongly charged line.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00110", "EV-TRIP-00110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if the rider's figures were accepted and a material deviation found, POL-RD-06's pattern test fails: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 744 completed_trips_90d, so no pattern is established and neither the FULL_REFUND uplift nor the conduct referral follows. POL-GEN-01 confines that test to deviation_flags_90d and makes the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter context only.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The disposition that protects the driver is to leave the charge standing: the rider filed, fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, so NO_ACTION preserves the fare the driver earned under POL-GEN-03. And on no view does the rider recover — POL-RD-07(iii) directs that a claim left unproven by an impaired trace be held rather than paid, and POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at the 0.39 weight the deciding distance carries. Disclosed: EV-GPS-00110 is IMPAIRED (GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE) at weight 0.39.",
